SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ssiiggppaauussee() function is implemented for compatibility with historic
     4.3BSD applications.  An incompatible interface by the same name, which
     used a single signal number rather than a mask, was present in AT&T
     System V UNIX, and was copied from there into the XX//OOppeenn SSyysstteemm
     IInntteerrffaacceess (XSI) option of IEEE Std 1003.1-2001 (“POSIX.1”).  FreeBSD im‐
     plements it under the name xxssii__ssiiggppaauussee().  The ssiigghhoolldd(), ssiiggiiggnnoorree(),
     ssiiggrreellssee() and ssiiggsseett() functions are implemented for compatibility with
     SSyysstteemm VV and XXSSII interfaces.

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ssiiggppaauussee() function appeared in 4.2BSD and has been deprecated.  All
     other functions appeared in FreeBSD 8.1 and were deprecated before being
     implemented.

